==============================================================================
  TARGETS NEEDED to stay within 5 mm of the planned path
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  hinge_area_right     execute_path     movej:   160   movel:   160
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Read this carefully: the MAX deviations for movej and movel are
  nearly identical at every count. At coarse spacing the error is
  dominated by the surface CURVING between targets — both commands
  cut that corner the same way. Target DENSITY is the lever, not the
  command.
  movel wins consistently on MEAN deviation (~2x), because along
  near-flat stretches a straight Cartesian segment already IS the
  path while a joint-linear move bows away from it. That is a real
  advantage for wipe quality — it is just not what sets the count.

